Subject: [PATCH 33/67] =?UTF-8?q?fix(aligram):=20claimJobsForFile=20atomic?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ity=20=E2=80=94=20transaction=20via=20caller=20runInTransaction?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20(Phase=203.2)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 43633746250 proved Room 2.8.4 ignores @Transaction on DAO
default methods: scenario 12 failed with the first UPDATE committed
in autocommit (ComparisonFailure at the rollback assertion), while
scenarios 11 and 13 passed — the exact signature of 'annotation
ignored'. The fix:
- PreservedRefDao: @Transaction removed from the default method
  (misleading); new static helper claimJobsInTransaction(db, ...)
  provides the transaction via db.runInTransaction — the ONLY way
  to call the claim. nextRevisionSeq shares the pattern but is
  read-only (single SELECT, no writes), so it needs no fix.
- AliGramPreservation.onFileLoadedInternal (the single production
  call site): claims through the helper.
- Scenarios 11/12/13 now call the helper (the production path);
  scenario 12's comment records that its original bare form is
  what failed on run 43633746250. Scenario 5(b) was already correct
  (claim nested in an outer runInTransaction); its comment fixed.
